\dotfile dox/example_web_fusion.dot "Transitive fusion of overlapping live ranges"

</div>

---

@section ext_t6 Error Handling, CLI, and Testing

@subsection ext_t6_cli CLI

The application supports:

- an interactive menu (`./register_alloc`);
- the batch interface:
  `./register_alloc -b ranges.txt config.txt allocation.txt`

Batch mode now returns a non-zero exit code when one of the input files cannot be
parsed, which makes the test script dependable.

@subsection ext_t6_tests Testing

The test suite has three goals:

- verify parsing and output formatting corner cases;
- pin down the interference and web-fusion semantics;
- validate the behaviour of all four allocation modes.

The integration tests use the six baseline datasets plus dedicated spilling, splitting, and free scenarios.
*/
